Subject: [PATCH] rp23xx/cyw43439: encode the PIO receive counter correctly

The receive loop samples a bit before executing JMP Y--, so its initial
counter must be the requested bit count minus one. The existing setup
rounds to the word-DMA extent but clocks one extra receive bit. Preserve
that extent and the F1 dummy word, and correct only the loop counter.

The native before/after witness executes the actual setup statements and
models the actual IN/JMP Y-- loop. The pinned Pico SDK 2.1.1 also encodes
its RX count minus one. This does not establish the cause of every radio
failure; hardware qualification remains separate.

Reference: https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-sdk/blob/2.1.1/src/rp2_common/pico_cyw43_driver/cyw43_bus_pio_spi.c#L256

--- a/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_cyw43439.c
+++ b/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_cyw43439.c
@@ -699,9 +699,11 @@
   rp23xx_pio_sm_put(rp_io->pio, rp_io->pio_sm, 31);
   rp23xx_pio_sm_exec(rp_io->pio, rp_io->pio_sm, pio_encode_out(pio_x, 32));
 
-  /* RX bit length is 32 bits for each 4 bytes requested. */
+  /* Y-- executes one more iteration than its initial value. Round the
+   * receive extent to DMA words, then encode that bit count minus one.
+   */
 
-  bit_length = 32 * ((length + 3) / 4);
+  bit_length = 32 * ((length + 3) / 4) - 1;
 
   /* For F1 reads add 32 bits for delay */
 
